<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sidi Fredj</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sidi Ferruch</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sidi Fredj, known to the French as Sidi Ferruch, is a small peninsula on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast about 25 km west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>. On 14 June 1830 a French army of more than 30,000 men under General de Bourmont landed there, defeated the dey's forces at Staouéli and advanced on Algiers, which capitulated on 5 July, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-conquest-of-algeria">French conquest of Algeria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sidi-fredj.jpg" alt="Sidi Fredj" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sandervalya · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sidi-Ferruch_le_26_Juin_2013_(Alger).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
